{
  "id": "c9",
  "title": "Recursion",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "c9-l1",
      "title": "A Function That Calls Itself",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A function can call itself. That's recursion: solve a big problem by solving a smaller version of the same problem.",
        "Every recursive function needs a base case, a situation simple enough to answer directly. Without it, the function calls itself forever, until the stack overflows and Unix stops the program.",
        "A countdown: to count down from n, print n, then count down from n − 1. Stop when n is 0."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "#include <stdio.h>",
          "",
          "void countdown(int n) {",
          "    if (n == 0) {",
          "        printf(\"liftoff\\n\");",
          "        return;",
          "    }",
          "    printf(\"%d\\n\", n);",
          "    countdown(n - 1);",
          "}",
          "",
          "int main() {",
          "    countdown(3);",
          "    return 0;",
          "}"
        ],
        "output": [
          "3",
          "2",
          "1",
          "liftoff"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "c9-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is recursion?",
          "options": [
            "A function that calls itself",
            "A loop with break",
            "A function with no return",
            "Two programs running at once"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Each call works on a smaller version of the problem."
        },
        {
          "id": "c9-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is the base case?",
          "options": [
            "The case simple enough to answer without calling itself again",
            "The first line of main",
            "The biggest input",
            "An error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "It's where the recursion stops."
        },
        {
          "id": "c9-l1-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What happens without a base case?",
          "options": [
            "The function calls itself until the stack overflows",
            "It returns 0",
            "It runs once",
            "The compiler fixes it"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Unix answers with a segmentation fault."
        },
        {
