          "prompt": "This program crashes. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "#include <stdio.h>",
            "",
            "void down(int n) {",
            "    if (n == 0)",
            "        return;",
            "    down(n + 1);",
            "}",
            "",
            "int main() {",
            "    down(3);",
            "    return 0;",
            "}"
          ],
          "answer": 5,
          "explanation": "n grows instead of shrinking, so it never reaches the base case 0. It must be down(n - 1)."
